# This project is its own pnpm workspace root, and says so on purpose.
#
# pnpm finds a workspace by walking UP from the current directory until it
# hits a `pnpm-workspace.yaml`. A project scaffolded into `workspaces/<name>`
# sits inside black-smith's tree, so without this file `pnpm install` here
# would resolve to whatever workspace root stands above it: the factory's
# lockfile gets rewritten, the project's dependencies get linked into the
# factory's `node_modules`, and every gate afterwards measures a toolchain the
# project does not own (P9-16c). While the factory declared a root of its own
# with no `packages`, that same walk killed `pnpm install` outright with
# ERR_PNPM_INVALID_WORKSPACE_CONFIGURATION before it resolved a single
# dependency (P9-19).
#
# `.` is the whole list: one package, this one. It stays correct once the
# project moves to its own remote, where there is nothing above it to find.
# Add entries here if this project ever grows a monorepo of its own.
packages:
  - '.'
